<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

  <!-- Combat Extended (CETeam.CombatExtended) compat: retunes the armor-penetration and mass
       traits to CE's model. Loaded only from the CE root (LoadFolders.xml), so nothing here runs
       without CE. The C# half, Source/1.6/Patches/CombatExtended/ (CombatExtendedCompat.cs plus
       one file per hook), carries the full account of why CE's verb bypasses the vanilla trait
       patches; this header covers only the def-level choices.

       Why the AP traits move. CE never calls VerbProperties.AdjustedArmorPenetration, the getter
       our per-tool armorPenetrationFactor / armorPenetrationQualityFloor fields hook; penetration
       comes from each ToolCE's own sharp (mm RHA) and blunt (MPa) numbers, multiplied by the
       weapon's MeleePenetrationFactor stat (CE's Stats_Weapons_Melee.xml: Weapon category, default
       1, StatPart_Quality 0.65 Awful to 1.5 Legendary, plus CE's stuff factors: plasteel 1.25,
       uranium 1.3, obsidian 1.15, wood 0.5). That stat is read with GetStatValue on the equipment,
       so a trait statFactors entry reaches it exactly like MeleeWeapon_DamageMultiplier does, shows
       in CE's own AP readout and prints as a vanilla stat line, all with no C#. Each trait keeps
       the shape its vanilla identity settled (its own header): a "+X on what the blade has" trait
       is a factor, weapon-wide here because the stat is; a "guaranteed baseline" trait is a floor
       stated at Normal quality and scaled by CE's quality ladder, in CE units, through the
       ceArmorPenetration*QualityFloor fields the C# hook reads. The vanilla fields are STRIPPED,
       not left beside the CE ones: TraitEffectSummary derives the info-card lines from them, and
       under CE those lines would promise a vanilla percentage the game never applies.

       The numbers, against CE's ladder (sharp, mm RHA: knife 0.32 to 0.42, gladius 0.43 to 0.48,
       longsword edge 0.72 and point 2.0, spear 2.25, axe 1.57, monosword 18 edge / 25 point,
       plasma sword 24 to 32; blunt, MPa: mace head 5.625, breach axe 3.375, warhammer 11.25.
       Armor, sharp: flak vest 8, recon 16, marine 20, cataphract 28):
       - Razored x1.25, a plasteel's worth and a mid-ladder step; slightly under the vanilla x1.3
         because it now also reaches the point and handle. A steel longsword edge becomes an
         untraited plasteel one and still fails a flak vest.
       - NeedlePoint x1.3, the vanilla number carried over.
       - ArmorSpike: Stab floor 3 mm RHA, just above the spear point's 2.25 as vanilla's 0.6 sits
         just above its 0.5, and far below a monosword.
       - Flanged: Blunt floor 8 MPa, a mace head lifted toward warhammer territory; dead on the
         warhammer itself, as vanilla's is on uranium and jade heads, accepted.
       - Monomolecular: the monosword's two tools verbatim, Cut 18 / Stab 25. The one vanilla entry
         covering both capacities becomes two, because CE's edge and point differ (25x and 12.5x a
         longsword's, so no single factor could be both) and a MeleeToolMod holds one sharp floor.
         At Masterwork (x1.35) that is 24.3 / 33.8: the edge beats marine and fails cataphract,
         the point beats cataphract. Legendary (x1.5): 27 / 37.5.
       - HeadWeighted loses its whole MeleeToolModExtension: its 1/1.3 AP factor exists only to
         cancel MeleeWeapon_DamageMultiplier's vanilla AP side effect, and under CE that stat does
         not touch penetration at all.
       The ArmorSpike and Flanged numbers are ladder-derived, not play-tested; tune here and keep
       this comment current.

       Bulk: CE's inventory stat, inherited from each base through ParentName. Lightweight and
       Cumbersome mirror their Mass factors onto it (CE's own Odyssey patch gives the barrel traits
       Bulk factors, the precedent), and so does LeadLined (Royalty root, 1.1). The eltex pair's
       psychic stats need nothing: CE patches no part of the gear-stat path (audited 2026-11-03).
       Bulk carries a StatPart, so it is never per-thing immutable, and its readers are inventory
       events, not ticks.

       On-hit payloads (audited 2026-11-03 against CE 16.7.4.0; the C# hook delivers them, this
       is what CE does to them once delivered; the ragged-wound mirrors are in HediffDefs_CE.xml):
       - PlasmaCored: Flame is "ambient" under CE (DamageDefExtensionCE on Core's Flame), so
         ArmorUtilityCE ignores the payload's AP and scales the 5 by one minus the summed Heat armor
         over the part (CE flak 0.25, power armor 0.5), floored: 2 to 3 points. The ignition is
         untouched (DamageWorker_Flame still attaches fire), but burning is roughly twice as
         damaging under CE (Fire.DoFireDamage's constant doubled and scaled by body size; Burn pain
         0.01875 -> 0.025, InfecterCE 0.07/h, scar x1.5). CE retuned the plasmasword our trait
         halves from Flame 10 @ 50% to 5 @ 30% on the
         edge (3 @ 20% on the point), so the chance follows it to 0.3 below; the amount already
         equals CE's edge value. The summary line is derived from the def, so the card follows.
       - ZeusHeaded: nothing patched, by decision (2026-11-03), and its vanilla header's
         self-limiting claim is vanilla-only. CE gives EMP the Electric armor category (no Core
         apparel or mechanoid carries any, so the 4 lands whole), replaces
         StunHandler.Notify_DamageApplied so the adaptation window is amount x 45 x body size
         instead of 2200t and a hit inside it re-stuns with at least 85% probability, and
         postfixes it with an Electrical hit (AP 9999, ElectricalBurn) worth the EMP amount on a
         mechanoid and a quarter of it on flesh. So under CE a zeus-headed mace stuns a mechanoid
         120t on nearly every hit, continuously at the mace head's 114t cooldown, plus 4
         electrical damage, and a human takes a 1-point burn per hit. The open question was a
         CE-root chance gate restoring the vanilla "one stun, then adaptation" cadence. Decided
         against, for four reasons. (1) Per hit the trait sits inside CE's own zeushammer envelope
         (CE's Royalty patch: head EMP 5 at 100% on a 147t cooldown, so a 150t stun re-applied
         every 147t and 5 electrical per hit; ours is 4, 120t, 114t): CE tuned that lock
         deliberately for its EMP melee, and a CE player who owns a zeushammer already has it.
         (2) CE's EMP model is deterministic delivery with probabilistic adaptation; a per-hit
         proc roll would make this the one EMP source in a CE game that fires at random, the
         opposite of what this root is for. (3) The self-limiting chain was a property vanilla's
         adaptation lends every EMP source, not the trait's identity, which is "an electromagnetic
         discharge on impact" and holds under CE. (4) The trait is already bounded by the Royalty
         root, commonality 0.5, the war merchant's ultratech ban and the Head token, and its
         +75 market value is a vanilla-side number CE gives no anchor for (CE does not reprice
         traits), so it stays. What would reopen it: CE changing the zeushammer to a chance or a
         smaller amount; mirror that here, as PlasmaCored mirrors the plasmasword.
       - Envenomed: ported to CE's wound-borne venom (2026-11-03). CE strips ToxicBuildup from
         vanilla's melee venoms (ScratchToxic, ToxicBite) and routes them through venom-carrying
         injuries feeding its VenomBuildup; DamageDefs_CE.xml does the same to UMW_Stab_Tox
         (injury UMW_VenomousStab, ToxicBuildup entry removed) and HediffDefs_CE.xml gives that
         injury CE's venom comp with CE's numbers. Nothing changes on the trait itself: amount 3
         at 50%, armor ignored (CE keeps vanilla's IgnoreArmor guard), fleshOnly false (a
         mechanoid takes a Crack, which carries no venom, so the flesh gate is CE's own). The dose
         math and the main-tree placement of the def are in 1.6/Defs/HediffDefs/VenomousStab.xml.

       Wording and readouts (audited 2026-11-03; what a CE player reads against what CE does):
       - The info card follows the reroute by construction: TraitEffectSummary derives the
         payload clause from the DamageDef, so Envenomed reads "applies toxic buildup" in vanilla
         and "leaving a venomous stab wound" under CE. The vanilla description was reworded to
         name neither mechanic ("poisons those it wounds").
       - Trait descriptions' armor wording (Razored, ArmorSpike, Flanged, Monomolecular) is
         qualitative and holds in both armor models; no description names a vanilla number.
       - Payload armor penetration: the UMW_TraitStat_ExtraDamageAP line prints a vanilla
         fraction, and under CE a non-ambient payload's DamageInfo AP is read in CE's units. No
         payload carries one today (the coatings ignore armor; EMP and Flame carry 0, and both are
         ambient under CE anyway), so a future payload with armorPenetration > 0 needs a CE-root
         value in CE units or the line lies. Worse than a lying line: a Sharp-category payload
         that neither ignores armor nor carries a CE-unit AP is DEFLECTED by CE against any
         armor at all (ArmorUtilityCE.TryPenetrateArmor deflects Sharp whenever armor > pen, and
         pen 0 counts as full pass-through only on a hit that was not deflected), and because
         our hook runs after CE has nulled LastAttackVerb the deflection logs "[CE] Deflection
         ... has null verb, overriding AP" per hit. A new Sharp payload must set ignoreArmor or
         ship a CE-root AP.
       - Opiated against CE's own Tranquilizer: CE's dart is a flat Consciousness 0.1 for 7500 to
         15000t at 0.9 severity per damage, i.e. one hit downs for 2 to 4 hours; ours builds over
         3 to 4 hits and holds the 0.7 downed threshold about 4.8 hours from a full dose. Slower
         to land, longer to hold, same order of magnitude, and CE's safer downed roll applies to
         both. Left alone: no CE anchor says ours is off.
       - BellCast against CE's crit stun: CE removes BluntBase's blunt-stun curves and stuns for
         25% of a non-Sharp crit's damage x 30t on flesh (a mace head's 15 is about 112t), so
         BellCast's 120t at 25% on any wounding hit, flesh and mechanoid alike, is the one
         non-crit blunt stun in a CE game and lands via StunFor, outside CE's re-stun and
         electrical postfix. Left alone: the same magnitude as CE's own, on a gate CE lacks. On
         a CE crit both can roll; StunFor keeps the longer of the two, never the sum (the C#
         header's hook 1 explains why on-hit traits fire on CE crits at all).
       - Tool labels under CE, in non-English games (known, accepted 2026-11-03): CE renames two
         inherited tools, the spear's point to "head" (and adds a second shaft, key shaft-1) and
         the warcasket broadsword's blade to "edge", so our DefInjected keys for the old labels
         stop resolving (one aggregated translation warning in the log) and those three tools
         show their English labels on the info card. A CE-root DefInjected file would fix the
         card but cannot be validated: the checker demands every injection from the sidecar the
         probe dumps on a 1.7 boot, which can never load CE (1.6/Mods/CLAUDE.md). Revisit when
         official CE runs on 1.7 and the probe can boot it.
       - Envenomed against CE's own unique-trait precedent: CE's Odyssey patch keeps ToxRounds
         on ToxicBuildup (extraDamages Bullet_TraitTox 2, severityPerDamageDealt cut to 0.005,
         about 0.01 buildup per hit) while rerouting the melee venoms (ScratchToxic, ToxicBite)
         onto wounds; the two precedents UMW_Stab_Tox claimed 1:1 parity with diverge under CE,
         and the port followed the melee branch, whose dose per proc (0.4 to 0.7 VenomBuildup)
         is about 50x CE's ToxRounds anchor. DECIDED 2026-11-03 (spec Q13): the venom branch
         stays. ToxRounds stays on ToxicBuildup because CE has no venomous gunshot injury to
         route a bullet onto; every venom CE could put on a wound, it did, its own arrow
         included, so the shortcut is not a balance anchor for melee. Per wound our 3-damage
         stab doses about a quarter of CE's venomous arrow (around 11 damage, lethal alone
         untended), and the counterplay (tend quality, ToxicResistance) is CE's own. The ranged
         branch would make the trait cosmetic under CE (a long fight reaches ToxicBuildup's
         first stage and stops). Reopened only by CE rerouting ToxRounds onto a wound or
         changing its venom comp numbers; the ranged branch (keep ToxicBuildup, cut
         severityPerDamageDealt) remains the one-operation alternative.
       - CE's melee tooltip shows Quilloned's parry through Hook 3 and CE's AP readout shows the
         factor traits; the floors show only in our trait block (the C# header). Nothing else of
         ours reaches a CE readout.

       Royalty traits sit under a PatchOperationConditional on node existence, like
       AddNameToBaseMeleeWeapons.xml does for the Royalty bases, so this root never depends on the
       Royalty root being present. The statFactors additions are conditional on the node existing
       so a future vanilla-side statFactors entry cannot produce a duplicate node. -->

  <!-- Razored: Cut AP x1.3 -> weapon-wide MeleePenetrationFactor x1.25. The Cut damageFactor stays. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationRemove">
    <xpath>Defs/WeaponTraitDef[defName="UMW_Razored"]/modExtensions/li[@Class="UniqueMeleeWeapons.MeleeToolModExtension"]/mods/li/armorPenetrationFactor</xpath>
  </Operation>
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/WeaponTraitDef[defName="UMW_Razored"]/statFactors</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/WeaponTraitDef[defName="UMW_Razored"]/statFactors</xpath>
      <value>
        <MeleePenetrationFactor>1.25</MeleePenetrationFactor>
      </value>
    </match>
    <nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/WeaponTraitDef[defName="UMW_Razored"]</xpath>
      <value>
        <statFactors>
          <MeleePenetrationFactor>1.25</MeleePenetrationFactor>
        </statFactors>
      </value>
    </nomatch>
  </Operation>

  <!-- NeedlePoint: Stab AP x1.3 -> weapon-wide MeleePenetrationFactor x1.3. The Stab damageFactor
       and the UMW_Stab_Deep conversion stay (the conversion needs the C# hook). -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationRemove">
    <xpath>Defs/WeaponTraitDef[defName="UMW_NeedlePoint"]/modExtensions/li[@Class="UniqueMeleeWeapons.MeleeToolModExtension"]/mods/li/armorPenetrationFactor</xpath>
  </Operation>
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/WeaponTraitDef[defName="UMW_NeedlePoint"]/statFactors</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/WeaponTraitDef[defName="UMW_NeedlePoint"]/statFactors</xpath>
      <value>
        <MeleePenetrationFactor>1.3</MeleePenetrationFactor>
      </value>
    </match>
    <nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/WeaponTraitDef[defName="UMW_NeedlePoint"]</xpath>
      <value>
        <statFactors>
          <MeleePenetrationFactor>1.3</MeleePenetrationFactor>
        </statFactors>
      </value>
    </nomatch>
  </Operation>

  <!-- ArmorSpike: Stab quality floor 0.6 -> 3 mm RHA at Normal, CE-quality-scaled. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <xpath>Defs/WeaponTraitDef[defName="UMW_ArmorSpike"]/modExtensions/li[@Class="UniqueMeleeWeapons.MeleeToolModExtension"]/mods/li/armorPenetrationQualityFloor</xpath>
    <value>
      <ceArmorPenetrationSharpQualityFloor>3</ceArmorPenetrationSharpQualityFloor>
    </value>
  </Operation>

  <!-- Flanged: Blunt quality floor 0.45 -> 8 MPa at Normal, CE-quality-scaled. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <xpath>Defs/WeaponTraitDef[defName="UMW_Flanged"]/modExtensions/li[@Class="UniqueMeleeWeapons.MeleeToolModExtension"]/mods/li/armorPenetrationQualityFloor</xpath>
    <value>
      <ceArmorPenetrationBluntQualityFloor>8</ceArmorPenetrationBluntQualityFloor>
    </value>
  </Operation>

  <!-- HeadWeighted: the AP-cancel factor has nothing to cancel under CE; drop the extension. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationRemove">
    <xpath>Defs/WeaponTraitDef[defName="UMW_HeadWeighted"]/modExtensions/li[@Class="UniqueMeleeWeapons.MeleeToolModExtension"]</xpath>
  </Operation>

  <!-- Lightweight / Cumbersome: Bulk factors mirroring their Mass factors. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/WeaponTraitDef[defName="UMW_Lightweight"]/statFactors</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/WeaponTraitDef[defName="UMW_Lightweight"]/statFactors</xpath>
      <value>
        <Bulk>0.7</Bulk>
      </value>
    </match>
    <nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/WeaponTraitDef[defName="UMW_Lightweight"]</xpath>
      <value>
        <statFactors>
          <Bulk>0.7</Bulk>
        </statFactors>
      </value>
    </nomatch>
  </Operation>
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/WeaponTraitDef[defName="UMW_Cumbersome"]/statFactors</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/WeaponTraitDef[defName="UMW_Cumbersome"]/statFactors</xpath>
      <value>
        <Bulk>1.3</Bulk>
      </value>
    </match>
    <nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/WeaponTraitDef[defName="UMW_Cumbersome"]</xpath>
      <value>
        <statFactors>
          <Bulk>1.3</Bulk>
        </statFactors>
      </value>
    </nomatch>
  </Operation>

  <!-- LeadLined (Royalty root): Bulk factor mirroring its Mass factor, inside the node-existence
       conditional every Royalty-root op carries. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/WeaponTraitDef[defName="UMW_LeadLined"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationConditional">
      <xpath>Defs/WeaponTraitDef[defName="UMW_LeadLined"]/statFactors</xpath>
      <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
        <xpath>Defs/WeaponTraitDef[defName="UMW_LeadLined"]/statFactors</xpath>
        <value>
          <Bulk>1.1</Bulk>
        </value>
      </match>
      <nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
        <xpath>Defs/WeaponTraitDef[defName="UMW_LeadLined"]</xpath>
        <value>
          <statFactors>
            <Bulk>1.1</Bulk>
          </statFactors>
        </value>
      </nomatch>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- PlasmaCored (Royalty root): Flame proc 50% -> 30%, CE's plasmasword edge chance. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/WeaponTraitDef[defName="UMW_PlasmaCored"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>Defs/WeaponTraitDef[defName="UMW_PlasmaCored"]/modExtensions/li[@Class="UniqueMeleeWeapons.MeleeTraitEffectExtension"]/onHitEffects/li[def="Flame"]/chance</xpath>
      <value>
        <chance>0.3</chance>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- Monomolecular (Royalty root): Cut+Stab quality floor 0.9 -> Cut 18 / Stab 25 mm RHA at
       Normal, as two entries. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/WeaponTraitDef[defName="UMW_Monomolecular"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>Defs/WeaponTraitDef[defName="UMW_Monomolecular"]/modExtensions/li[@Class="UniqueMeleeWeapons.MeleeToolModExtension"]/mods</xpath>
      <value>
        <mods>
          <li>
            <capacities>
              <li>Cut</li>
            </capacities>
            <ceArmorPenetrationSharpQualityFloor>18</ceArmorPenetrationSharpQualityFloor>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacities>
              <li>Stab</li>
            </capacities>
            <ceArmorPenetrationSharpQualityFloor>25</ceArmorPenetrationSharpQualityFloor>
          </li>
        </mods>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
